.TH SDL_AsyncIOFromFile 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_AsyncIOFromFile \- Use this function to create a new
.BR SDL_AsyncIO
object for reading from and/or writing to a named file.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_asyncio.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_AsyncIO * SDL_AsyncIOFromFile(const char *file, const char *mode);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR mode
string understands the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dqr\(dq: Open a file for reading only\[char46] It must exist\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqw\(dq: Open a file for writing only\[char46] It will create missing files or truncate existing ones\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqr+\(dq: Open a file for update both reading and writing\[char46] The file must exist\[char46]
.PP
\(bu \(dqw+\(dq: Create an empty file for both reading and writing\[char46] If a file with the same name already exists its content is erased and the file is treated as a new empty file\[char46]
.PP
There is no \(dqb\(dq mode, as there is only \(dqbinary\(dq style I/O, and no \(dqa\(dq mode for appending, since you specify the position when starting a task\[char46]
.PP
This function supports Unicode filenames, but they must be encoded in UTF-8 format, regardless of the underlying operating system\[char46]
.PP
This call is _not_ asynchronous; it will open the file before returning, under the assumption that doing so is generally a fast operation\[char46] Future reads and writes to the opened file will be async, however\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I file
a UTF-8 string representing the filename to open\[char46]
.TP
.I mode
an ASCII string representing the mode to be used for opening the file\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to the
.BR SDL_AsyncIO
structure that is created or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_CloseAsyncIO (3),
.BR SDL_ReadAsyncIO (3),
.BR SDL_WriteAsyncIO (3)
